    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 60 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved the owner's date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starting 1 July), touching three files.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** (OwnerDto schema, from which the DTO is generated)\n- Added a new read-only `fiscalYear` property (`FY<YY>`).\n- Updated the `membershipNumber`, `membershipPoints`, and `membershipLevel` descriptions to reflect the fiscal-year basis.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`**\n- Added `getFiscalYear()` returning `FY<YY>` from the (business-day-adjusted) `registrationDate`, plus a private `fiscalYearOf(LocalDate)` helper. A date on/after 1 July belongs to that year's fiscal year; an earlier date belongs to the previous year's, and `YY` is the last two digits of the fiscal year's starting calendar year.\n- Changed `getMembershipNumber()`'s `-M<YY>` segment to use the fiscal year instead of the calendar year (keeping it consistent with `fiscalYear`).\n- Changed the tenure component of `getMembershipPoints()` from a 365-day window to elapsed fiscal years (`+3` when the registration date's fiscal year precedes the current one).\n\nMapStruct auto-maps the new `getFiscalYear()` getter onto the generated DTO field, so no mapper/controller changes were needed.\n\n**Behaviour notes**\n- `fiscalYear` and `membershipNumber` are derived from the same fiscal-year computation, satisfying Cp14's consistency check and Cp48's format check.\n- New owners are still in the current fiscal year \u2192 zero tenure points, so Cp39/Cp40 (max level 3 / specific points for fresh owners) continue to hold.\n- I used the \"start-year\" fiscal-year label (a date in Aug 2026 \u2192 `FY26`), matching the spec's emphasis that the fiscal year *starts* on 1 July. No test pins the absolute FY value \u2014 they only require internal consistency \u2014 but this reading is the most faithful to the wording.\n\nThe full suite (60 tests) is green.",
